{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"18814b70-8b7e-4c43-946c-5c9dac496990","agentId":"af0587f74b82ee0e0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers. Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no COM3; TestClient only. Report under 80 words. Others own report_routes/report.html, fullscan.html, handbook 07: do not touch. You own cuore/web/templates/tests.html, static/tests.css, tests.js, cuore/services/tests_bridge.py, mes-log-mcp/mes/mechanic_tests.py (additive), cuore/tests/check_tests_page.py (extend). You may commit and push (`github` main only; never koch-mcp/).\n\n1. Each test row on /v/{vin}/tests gets \"Print this test\": a print view /v/{vin}/tests/{id}/print — one page, as-of stamp, vehicle, the procedure steps as a tick list, pass criteria with sources and confidence, hazards, a results box (Pass/Fail/Inconclusive/Not possible, value, unit, notes, by, date) matching the fields the result form stores. Print stylesheet, 12pt body.\n2. Add the ESIM commanded test to the catalogue (additive, sourced from the repo's own ESIM/Test A documents and cuore/live/actuators or the MES actuator list — grep -l \"ESIM\" cuore/live mes-log-mcp/mes once): id esim_commanded_vent_test: with the engine running and purge active, command the ESIM vent closed (MES actuator test, or wiTECH; in CUORE it is MCP-only and needs the consent phrase ACTUATE ECM <name> — state that in the procedure), watch the ESIM switch parameter and vacuum build; pass = switch reports sealed within the ECM's own window (limits come from the car: Mode 06 MID 3A); fail = no vacuum (vent not sealing: solenoid, driver circuit, connector) or vacuum but no switch change (switch/signal path). Link it as the second step after evap_test_a_esim_switch in both tests' when_to_use text; systems [\"evap\", \"electrical_supply\"]; confidences as the sources allow, UNKNOWN where no number is on file.\n3. The Tests page's \"Recommended for this car\" must list Test A first, then the ESIM commanded test, then the wiring test, when P0440/P0455/P0456 are active and the ESIM hypothesis is open (rank by the fault tree's next test, then by supports_hypotheses match).\nTests: print view 200 with the tick list and results box; catalogue has esim_commanded_vent_test with valid keys; recommended order with the live fixture (copy 2026-10-13 lines from C:\\ProgramData\\cuore\\observations.jsonl at test time; never modify it). Run check_tests_page.py, check_jobs_rules.py, check_screens.py. Commit \"Tests: printable test sheets; ESIM commanded vent test; EVAP recommended order\" with the Co-Authored-By line, push, report the hash."},"uuid":"7c91ebb3-5872-46de-a4e2-b9fca4dad1e6","timestamp":"2026-10-14T05:30:05.788Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
