 a scan tool \"\n        \"without MCP\",\n        \"scan tool live data: the ESIM/EVAP switch parameter (see \"\n        \"cuore.live.channels -- no readable OBD DID exists for it; the reading \"\n        \"comes only from the actuator-test screen or wiTECH live data), \"\n        \"evap_vapor_pressure_abs, commanded_evap_purge, fuel_level\"],\n  procedure=[\n      \"Confirm fuel level is in the 15-85% EVAP-verification window.\",\n      \"Start the engine and let it idle until the EVAP purge monitor is actively \"\n      \"purging (commanded_evap_purge > 0% on live data).\",\n      \"In CUORE this step is MCP-only: command the ESIM/EVAP vent solenoid closed \"\n      \"through the obd2 run_actuator tool (or the MES Actuators tab / wiTECH), \"\n      \"which refuses the command unless the operator states the consent phrase \"\n      \"exactly as 'ACTUATE ECM <name>' (the actuator's own name).\",\n      \"With the vent held closed and purge still running, watch for vacuum to \"\n      \"build (evap_vapor_pressure_abs) and for the ESIM/EVAP switch parameter to \"\n      \"report sealed.\",\n      \"Command the vent back open; confirm vacuum bleeds down and the switch \"\n      \"parameter returns to its baseline (not-sealed) state.\",\n      \"Record whether the switch changed within the ECM's own reported window, \"\n      \"not a number from this catalogue.\",\n  ],\n  pass_criteria=[_pc(\n      \"ESIM/EVAP switch parameter vs. vacuum build, vent commanded closed, \"\n      \"engine running and purging\",\n      \"switch reports sealed within the ECM's own measured-value/limit window\",\n      \"\", \"SAE J1979 Appendix D / ISO 15031-5 Mode $06 MID 0x3A (0.090\\\" leak) \"\n          \"definition (cuore.live.mode06); the numeric window is the ECU's own, \"\n          \"read back from Mode $06 MID 3A, not a figure in this catalogue\",\n          UNKNOWN)],\n  fail_means=\"No vacuum builds: the vent itself is not sealing -- solenoid, its \"\n             \"driver circuit, or the connector. Vacuum builds but the switch \"\n             \"never reports sealed: the fault is in the switch or its signal \"\n             \"path (connector, wiring, ECU input), not the vent hardware -- the \"\n             \"same signal-path hypothesis wiTECH Test A targets.\",\n  related_codes=[\"P0440\", \"P0455\", \"P0456\"],\n  supports_hypotheses=[\"EVAP: ESIM signal path\", \"EVAP valve stuck\", \"EVAP leak\"],\n  refutes_hypotheses=[\"EVAP: ESIM signal path\", \"EVAP valve stuck\"],\n  duration_min=15,\n  safety=\"HTTP surface is read-only; this test is only available through the MCP \"\n         \"actuator-control tool (or MES/wiTECH bidirectional control), never \"\n         \"through the HTTP job/tests API -- it writes a live command to the car \"\n         \"and is refused without the operator stating the consent phrase exactly \"\n         \"as 'ACTUATE ECM <name>'. Fuel vapor at the canister/wheel well -- no \"\n         \"sparks or open flame.\",\n  hazards=[\"fuel vapor\", \"electrical\"])\n\n_t(\"esim_bench_test\", \"ESIM bench test\", \"emissions\", [\"evap\"],\n  _applies(grecale=False),","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":293,"oldLines":6,"newStart":293,"newLines":69,"lines":["          \"at the canister/wheel well -- no sparks or open flame.\",","   hazards=[\"fuel vapor\"])"," ","+_t(\"esim_commanded_vent_test\", \"ESIM commanded vent test\", \"emissions\",","+  [\"evap\", \"electrical_supply\"], _applies(grecale=False),","+  purpose=\"Second step on the ESIM signal-path line, right after wiTECH Test A \"","+          \"(evap_test_a_esim_switch): with the engine running and purge active, \"","+          \"command the ESIM vent closed through the scan tool's actuator control \"","+          \"rather than a hand pump, and watch both the switch parameter and \"","+          \"whether vacuum actually builds -- corroborates Test A's hand-pump \"","+          \"result under real operating vacuum, in one pass.\",","+  car_state=\"KOER\",","+  when_to_use=\"Run as the second step after wiTECH Test A (evap_test_a_esim_switch) \"","+              \"-- whether Test A passed, failed, or wasn't available (no wiTECH on \"","+              \"hand) -- before the ESIM wiring test or any further parts purchase. \"","+              \"In CUORE this test is MCP-only and needs the consent phrase \"","+              \"ACTUATE ECM <name>; it is never available through the HTTP job/\"","+              \"tests API because it writes a live command to the car.\",","+  tools=[\"MCP obd2 run_actuator tool (consent phrase ACTUATE ECM <name>), or the \"","+        \"MES Actuators tab / wiTECH bidirectional control, for a scan tool \"","+        \"without MCP\",","+        \"scan tool live data: the ESIM/EVAP switch parameter (see \"","+        \"cuore.live.channels -- no readable OBD DID exists for it; the reading \"","+        \"comes only from the actuator-test screen or wiTECH live data), \"","+        \"evap_vapor_pressure_abs, commanded_evap_purge, fuel_level\"],","+  procedure=[","+      \"Confirm fuel level is in the 15-85% EVAP-verification window.\",","+      \"Start the engine and let it idle until the EVAP purge monitor is actively \"","+      \"purging (commanded_evap_purge > 0% on live data).\",","+      \"In CUORE this step is MCP-only: command the ESIM/EVAP vent solenoid closed \"","+      \"through the obd2 run_actuator tool (or the MES Actuators tab / wiTECH), \"","+      \"which refuses the command unless the operator states the consent phrase \"","+      \"exactly as 'ACTUATE ECM <name>' (the actuator's own name).\",","+      \"With the vent held closed and purge still running, watch for vacuum to \"","+      \"build (evap_vapor_pressure_abs) and for the ESIM/EVAP switch parameter to \"","+      \"report sealed.\",","+      \"Command the vent back open; confirm vacuum bleeds down and the switch \"","+      \"parameter returns to its baseline (not-sealed) state.\",","+      \"Record whether the switch changed within the ECM's own reported window, \"","+      \"not a number from this catalogue.\",","+  ],","+  pass_criteria=[_pc(","+      \"ESIM/EVAP switch parameter vs. vacuum build, vent commanded closed, \"","+      \"engine running and purging\",","+      \"switch reports sealed within the ECM's own measured-value/limit window\",","+      \"\", \"SAE J1979 Appendix D / ISO 15031-5 Mode $06 MID 0x3A (0.090\\\" leak) \"","+          \"definition (cuore.live.mode06); the numeric window is the ECU's own, \"","+          \"read back from Mode $06 MID 3A, not a figure in this catalogue\",","+          UNKNOWN)],","+  fail_means=\"No vacuum builds: the vent itself is not sealing -- solenoid, its \"","+             \"driver circuit, or the connector. Vacuum builds but the switch \"","+             \"never reports sealed: the fault is in the switch or its signal \"","+             \"path (connector, wiring, ECU input), not the vent hardware -- the \"","+             \"same signal-path hypothesis wiTECH Test A targets.\",","+  related_codes=[\"P0440\", \"P0455\", \"P0456\"],","+  supports_hypotheses=[\"EVAP: ESIM signal path\", \"EVAP valve stuck\", \"EVAP leak\"],","+  refutes_hypotheses=[\"EVAP: ESIM signal path\", \"EVAP valve stuck\"],","+  duration_min=15,","+  safety=\"HTTP surface is read-only; this test is only available through the MCP \"","+         \"actuator-control tool (or MES/wiTECH bidirectional control), never \"","+         \"through the HTTP job/tests API -- it writes a live command to the car \"","+         \"and is refused without the operator stating the consent phrase exactly \"","+         \"as 'ACTUATE ECM <name>'. Fuel vapor at the canister/wheel well -- no \"","+         \"sparks or open flame.\",","+  hazards=[\"fuel vapor\", \"electrical\"])","+"," _t(\"esim_bench_test\", \"ESIM bench test\", \"emissions\", [\"evap\"],","   _applies(grecale=False),","   purpose=\"Bench-check the ESIM's vacuum switch, internal seal and pressure relief \""]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"11fe7abf-110e-403e-b6ba-a9eb56209284","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3a42e272-5831-4b5c-a5ae-58e11ca1e7a4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
